+# Persistent ordinary history pairing policy Source proposal
+
+This package fixes a prospective policy before any new persistent Rust output.
+It contains no comparer, runner, engine, tests, expected values or canonical patch.
+The previously released Native05 A24 input and complete stream are reused only
+after their genuine QA/source/input/argv authorities are authenticated. Root owns
+all actual runs. Source review is not numerical or integration certification.
+
+Four semantic boundary families pair the selected Init/update inputs and actual
+returned endpoints. Each side first proves its own invocation/return/clock order.
+Native scopes/parent returns remain mandatory. Rust Begin/Commit/failure events
+are real caller witnesses, not invented Native checkpoints. A complete shared
+phase/day/hour/timestep/dt key must be unique on both sides. No ordinal zip,
+warmup trimming, kickoff filtering or environment inference is permitted.
+
+Actual names and relationships establish a bijection for Zone, Space,
+Construction and Surface owners. Full allocation, every fixed19 column/tail and
+independent HT/opaque/AllHT order remain required. Native material layer IDs have
+no captured name arena here; they remain honest unpaired context until an actual
+independent identity authority exists. Area and coefficient differences are
+reported after identity mapping, never used to prune the map.
+
+Every compared scalar family lists its actual field correspondence and literal
+Native/Rust Source bounds. Copies require exact IEEE bits/class. Finite arithmetic
+uses zero absolute/relative tolerance and exact class/shape/signed zero. Nonfinite
+arithmetic is required unavailable. This does not import the direct17 policy.
+The Source-bounded SUR04 inside equation requires actual positive-zero inactive
+operands and finite active input admission; no per-iteration pair is fabricated
+from history endpoint events. Outside/inside solver equivalence remains separate.
+
+Native environment/KickOff/calendar and Rust record-index/generation identities
+are retained optional context, never fabricated as shared keys. Required missing
+clock, ambiguous identity, extra/unmatched stage or partial owner blocks a selected
+paired claim. All matched/unmatched/unavailable/mismatch and optional-context rows
+must be retained uncapped. The existing four-GiB factual reader limit retains
+excess as failure; it cannot cap the producer or shorten the run.
+
+Header supplied the prospective typed event/schema contract; its final immutable
+exporter Source/serializer is not yet sealed. Its FULL correspondence review and
+actual runtime bindings are mandatory before use. Current Rust Source contexts
+are exact archives of the bytes at this seal, explicitly historical thereafter.
+No actual Rust/Native numerical outputs were read to choose this policy. The
+separate released whole-Init comparison review does not supply persistent inputs,
+values, counts or tolerances to this package. Gates remain unchanged.
